{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "08", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "04", "M": "44", "S": "39"}}, "news": [{"title": "Dharwad consumer panel orders builder to refund 83 plot buyers with 10% interest", "para": "In a significant ruling, a consumer commission has mandated a Hubballi developer to refund 83 buyers who purchased plots in the failed Sai Ram City layout. Despite receiving deposits and installment payments over two years, the developer neglected the promised development. The commission identified service deficiencies and unfair practices, ordering the developer to return the full amount with 10% annual interest and additional compensation.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/dharwad-consumer-panel-orders-builder-to-refund-83-plot-buyers-with-10-interest/133045996?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-109691/133045996.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "Andhra Pradesh government clears pilot slum redevelopment project in Visakhapatnam", "para": "The government of Andhra Pradesh has green-lighted the Velampeta slum redevelopment initiative in Visakhapatnam. This innovative project operates under a public-private partnership and a Design, Build, Finance, Transfer framework. Families from economically weaker sections will be relocated within the same area, while Transferable Development Rights will help to fill the funding void.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/andhra-pradesh-government-clears-pilot-slum-redevelopment-project-in-visakhapatnam/133045899?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-51754/133045899.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "Eye on high-rise work resumption, builders in Kolkata start calling back workers to sites", "para": "In Kolkata, construction developers are bringing laborers back to the sites as many halted projects gain the necessary approvals to restart. Contractors are reaching out to the workers who had previously returned home, signaling a resurgence in construction activity expected in just weeks. The industry is positive about the government's newly implemented safety standards, seeing them as a boost to the sector.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/eye-on-high-rise-work-resumption-builders-in-kolkata-start-calling-back-workers-to-sites/133045792?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-228203/133045792.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}]}